#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059566 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "7bfcfcbb-6212-5f9b-90aa-c79fbf7221e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4518" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](images/ed/ed434344208758284aa0f144676f7dd6498a63faeb0248d18e87c4be6c3d87f2.png)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/b9/b9364923447e278db5ec47bef74e1a05310645b30df22d4ea5efcc0de46c6ed2.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/16/16cb1608f70821d138f0c6984038bb42d86d9fbf76d560d94d2e25bd6fdb05e0.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/0a/0abbbaf34955fa40d6cdbfa9e16cb1567ee16271d65b4565206a0f2204eedf6d.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/4b/4b915439c3e9922d692aab4205a728160e0a1286f82fa5ebc736460901581147.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "c4af8b0d-e4ee-56f4-9cf6-594530639339" :question/math-academy-id "e-4519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](images/c9/c9b7abb2641034c1769c6fe6b13b96edd7ccc282b61424b2031a3d37faa456e4.png)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/6f/6f1bf319faf8be4a9a79c0a6f9301e6eac48a5b04f66949b679e8445b07e9d9c.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/fc/fc1ac06787ed64ebefbb1a7a82f9bf785525777f61831bbbc39bd25c7e629d5a.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/d0/d0249dcecf6b75cd6ff7c4623beac6fd6cfae64a58d043bb6759440167f40ea1.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/64/64d1f57717dda57c8a7fbc403728ee9699a22ce995f68a50a0b80f25543fdab6.png)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61b6213e-6630-5cbc-a2be-bba26537e9d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263842} {:answer/id #uuid "98683e89-44c4-5b63-a6a0-5143070e1a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=8,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264311} {:answer/id #uuid "a16f2ca2-4f2e-5acc-9b55-06d4bbfa6420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=8,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264374} {:answer/id #uuid "dc08dfd2-1ae1-53cb-adad-40873d7ac878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264916} {:answer/id #uuid "f9db3e03-47ba-53e0-8851-1e7f8c0aa7b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9db3e03-47ba-53e0-8851-1e7f8c0aa7b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265185} :answer-field/id #uuid "21ecd5d5-730f-53a8-b7fd-5892a28e6ac7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "718180b1-bf73-575f-add7-0f6c8d9bba0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130536" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ -6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85806f6e-3f8d-56f5-8841-0e3c0a47083a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85806f6e-3f8d-56f5-8841-0e3c0a47083a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298128} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f730fa1-b5c3-50b2-9976-270a3b0b824a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97ab1973-03cd-5f88-a18f-9217286fd9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97ab1973-03cd-5f88-a18f-9217286fd9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298209} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bda87eb-624b-5dc0-a615-09034a4dd617" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7150ff71-c085-5d5f-84bc-cd85d9ef931f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7150ff71-c085-5d5f-84bc-cd85d9ef931f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298040} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c396013-8c55-5d91-a811-c1d7554b13b5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91f9c034-96b3-537d-95ac-54136e6ff76c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91f9c034-96b3-537d-95ac-54136e6ff76c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298185} :answer-field/id #uuid "cda9e946-5a85-5e86-9781-1b1870f198bf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "193f944c-d77c-5446-9a05-12850a3f60de" :question/math-academy-id "q-316961" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-1$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43fddea3-d0f8-5695-aeca-4914b81fc7dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43fddea3-d0f8-5695-aeca-4914b81fc7dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297828} :answer-field/id #uuid "07d63cfd-2c70-56f1-91e5-6b0a54a598e7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e6f4ae6-5078-5a23-8d05-43bfab7668c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e6f4ae6-5078-5a23-8d05-43bfab7668c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297949} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d90e8c9-82f6-5108-bd2d-cc950fdc0758" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298741} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf2cb796-ed04-5c16-a021-89dd5f064140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf2cb796-ed04-5c16-a021-89dd5f064140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298391} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fe819ce-fd88-59b2-8385-d30f01206bb9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ca9278-0c20-567c-a5f8-c1e5fc82c7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09ca9278-0c20-567c-a5f8-c1e5fc82c7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297603} :answer-field/id #uuid "acafd20b-a624-534c-a948-7dfeb34188c8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "05df8d85-d4aa-50db-b657-3624538dbf63" :question/math-academy-id "q-316998" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2z-2y-5x=5 \\\\ -3z+3y+4x=1 \\\\ 2z-2x+y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $-5$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $4$ | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $2$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5x-2y+2z=5 \\\\ 4x+3y-3z=1 \\\\ -2x+y+2z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba42191e-a1b2-5cbe-be73-25f0fc307cc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba42191e-a1b2-5cbe-be73-25f0fc307cc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298362} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e6ea13-72da-5a50-9831-59f3bb32ec83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c62d600f-ef35-5c93-8a98-7c0b5d6bbb92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c62d600f-ef35-5c93-8a98-7c0b5d6bbb92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298418} :answer-field/id #uuid "525ad87c-5619-57d3-92a7-8525697b4703" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298915} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "861c6ed2-e966-5692-accb-b534f1e773b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "861c6ed2-e966-5692-accb-b534f1e773b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298131} :answer-field/id #uuid "88962de7-2fa7-50be-bcd3-a4e0c59688f8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299095} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "146371ee-1c0b-5294-90fc-369dd2c1ae84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "146371ee-1c0b-5294-90fc-369dd2c1ae84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297639} :answer-field/id #uuid "b029a4eb-3160-581a-8813-6eaf9bdeebd7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cdeadc34-e7f3-5a9c-9bba-7c02bc1cee1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-317632" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+4=7 \\\\ -2x+6z-1=8 \\\\ 7y-5z+2=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $5$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} | $6$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $9$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $7$ | $-5$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-5$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+0z=3 \\\\ -2x+0y+6z=9 \\\\ 0x+7y-5z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060276 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "099fa1e0-d872-5eb5-81ed-b3b1edaada04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321222} {:answer/id #uuid "138e861a-0cc2-58a9-9676-1ec3e92f91ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321303} {:answer/id #uuid "7024eba8-43e2-5236-ad74-99d0c32d9f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=-4,\\,c=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322019} {:answer/id #uuid "806f8895-3e66-5150-bdff-c12b2f1ea7b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=11,\\,c=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322157} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2f6adf-c8fe-58ac-9550-1c74ef4b3ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=11,\\,b=-4,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "099fa1e0-d872-5eb5-81ed-b3b1edaada04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321222} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbe13b71-8293-5712-8025-31df3dbc7ef9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5006a5f1-0a5e-50bb-a47b-7da41b1e709f" :question/math-academy-id "q-36181" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y+z=2 \\\\ x-6y+11z=3 \\\\ 3x-4y-z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & a \\\\ 1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "899af756-e049-505b-aca8-fcddbcc599a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=1,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343433} {:answer/id #uuid "9934f80a-4330-52c3-b892-b8e6146150ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343586} {:answer/id #uuid "a628bb7b-ab3e-5568-a237-263714a782db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343701} {:answer/id #uuid "c77edf43-1b15-5283-9e68-19790d9e948c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343990} {:answer/id #uuid "d9de4d48-ae2a-5b5a-848b-ea2b298a17cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=1,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a628bb7b-ab3e-5568-a237-263714a782db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343701} :answer-field/id #uuid "063b5447-f723-563a-b519-b068df6762ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8162803-a4d6-5f94-9721-2c47db8e7ec4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75506" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-y+z=1 \\\\ 2z+y+x=-1 \\\\ 3y-z+x=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & b \\\\ 1 & c & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-y+z=1 \\\\ x+y+2z=-1 \\\\ x+3y-z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=2,\\,c=3.$"}]}
